 to wait and see uh something  else that might be coming is this big  decision from the supreme court could  overturn roe v wade in virginia abortion  access is legal up to 25 weeks you've  talked about dialing it down to 20 weeks  if roe v wade is overturned what's going  to happen in your state well first what  we've been focused on is keeping our  justices safe and  this leak was done to cause chaos and  parading and picketing in front of the  justices homes in order to influence  them is wrong and so  we saw this assassination temp on  justice kavanaugh in maryland and it's  just kept us all very very on a  heightened awareness to make sure our  justices are safe and and this final  ruling will come down and if and if it's  delivered as expected my first job is to  keep virginians safe and so we're going  to protect our constitutional right to  protest if people want to protest and  demonstrate but we're also going to  enforce the law and make sure there's no  violence and so we've coordinated with  mayors and local police and state police  to make sure that people get to express  their constitutional rights but we're  going to keep people safe and if they  break the law we're going to but what  about women who may be worried about  their abortion rights i hear we all  agree we want everybody to be safe we  get that but no one wants to see  protesters outside supreme court  justices right home or them endangered  but what do you say to women in virginia  who may be worried  well first of all nothing changes  immediately in virginia uh and what  we're going to do is work with our  legislature i'm a pro-life governor and  i've got to work with our legislature to  to see the next path and so we'll start  those discussions um it's going to  require a cooperation between our  legislators and the governor in order to  get something done and we're going to  start that work so it sounds like you  don't really want to say until we know  exactly what the decision is going to be  yeah we don't know yet i mean i think  there's a lot of  supposition on what it's going to say  based on the based on the the leaked  draft opinion but we need to wait to see  what it says and then we'll work with  our legislature and go to and go to work  as a team from there so if you're  pro-life  can can we ask about that because i'm  worried about the clock ticking the the  january 6 committee hearings that are  going on right now where we've seen time  after time trump advisers telling the  president at the time listen you lost he  is still refusing to acknowledge that  even as we sit here today do you think  that's hurting your party and do you  believe first do you believe that joe  biden was elected president of this  country i i do believe that joe biden  was elected president of this country  and i think what happened on january 6  was awful awful um it's a it was a real  blight on our democracy  i have to be honest though i talk to  virginians every day and what they're  talking about is not january 6. what  they're talking about is runaway  inflation they're talking about gas  prices through the roof grocery prices  they're worried about crime in their  local neighborhoods we're all talking  about that governor but this is also  very important because there are so many  conflicting things where people say oh  it's just tourists that got out of  control it was not a big deal i mean i  do think it's important that the record  reflect accurately what happened do you  think it's hurting your republican party  well let me let me start again i think  the media cares a lot more about this  than the people that the people do and  we can tell i mean there's there's prime  time coverage and candidly not many  people are watching it and this is  because around the kitchen tables in  virginia and i think america it's  runaway inflation it's crime it's  schools these are the issues that  virginians and i think americans are  worried about and this is why thi